 # Changelog
 
+## 1.7.0 (2026-11-15)
+
+- Each ticket has a due time (`due`): its created time plus the response hours for its priority (4 for urgent, 24 for
+  high, 72 for normal, 168 for low). The hours are `DUE_HOURS_URGENT`, `DUE_HOURS_HIGH`, `DUE_HOURS_NORMAL` and
+  `DUE_HOURS_LOW`. A due time is set once: changing the hours or the ticket's priority does not move it.
+- Tickets already in the data file get a due time from their created time and priority, and keep it.
+- `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists the open and in-progress tickets whose due time has passed.
+- Until `DUE_TIMES=on`, the API is unchanged. The data file stays version 1, so 1.4.0 can still load a file this
+  release wrote.
+
+## 1.6.0 (2026-11-15)
+
+- `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent, or unassigns it.
+- Every ticket has an `assignee` (`null` when unassigned). `GET /tickets` filters by `assignee`.
+- The assigned agent is notified. The command line lists each ticket's assignee.
+
+## 1.5.0 (2026-11-15)
+
+- `POST /tickets/import` bulk-creates tickets (`{"tickets": [...]}`), all of a batch or none, at most 5000.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
