+## Due times
+
+Each ticket stores `due` (created time plus the `DUE_HOURS_*` for its priority). Existing tickets get that time from
+their own created time and priority the first time this release loads the data file, and keep it. The data file stays
+version 1: extra `due` fields are ignored by 1.4.0.
+
+Roll-out:
+
+1. Deploy this release with `DUE_TIMES` unset. The API is unchanged; the data file gains `due` on every ticket.
+2. Confirm the file holds `due`, then set `DUE_TIMES=on` and reload. Tickets include `due`, and `GET /tickets?overdue=true`
+   lists open and in-progress tickets past due.
+3. If that misbehaves, unset `DUE_TIMES` (the API is as it was) or go back to 1.4.0: it still starts on the file this
+   release wrote and shows every ticket.
+
+Change the hours with `DUE_HOURS_URGENT`, `DUE_HOURS_HIGH`, `DUE_HOURS_NORMAL` and `DUE_HOURS_LOW`. Already stored due
+times do not move.
+
 ## The command line and the weekly report
 
 `bin/tickets.js` and `scripts/weekly-report.js` read the data file and never write it, so they are safe to run beside
